! mcp_bootstrap_p243.strap -- MCP printed page 243: the R-section
! (Input Program end-of-job / rewrite) from LX,VP,VPD to RKCRWT NOP,RSAM1,
! lines 1-56.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.250, read at 400 dpi, 900 dpi for
! doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID ?B000071  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 243"; the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 227604, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, all located, contiguous from 227604.00 to
! 227642.00 (a half word; next location 227642.40).  No remarks and no
! comment cards.  The volume OCR puts p.242's last row (CM1111, a full
! word) at 227603.00, so line 1 joins it; p.244's line 1 reads 227642.40
! there, so line 56 joins the next page.  Asterisks after the LOCATION
! on lines 17 and 39.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 4 "RGOOD" / line 9 label "RGCCD": open round glyphs; written
!     RGOOD (English GOOD).  BZXVZ,RGOOD prints 227611.71 = line 9's
!     227611.40.  Nothing else references it -- rests on the word.
!   * line 34 label "RLCCPE", line 38 BXVGZ,RLCCPE: written RLOOPE
!     (LOOP); 227626.71 = line 34's 227626.40.  This page only.
!   * line 5 "CMOCOO" = CM0000 (connective 0000); line 5's h2 byte
!     prints "FC" with an open round in an octal-dropping row
!     ("001000.CC"); CM0000 assembles F0.
!   * line 13 "B,CMCP" = B,DMCP (worn D stem); 000040.10 = DMCP 32.0.
!   * line 14 "VF,CBSFL" = VF,DBSFL; prints 000007.00+ = DBSFL 7.0.
!   * line 31 "VWT" (sheet read VHT): 900 dpi shows W; same binary as
!     line 54 LVI,VU,VWT.  line 42 "VRQB" (sheet read VRQE): 900 dpi B.
!   * hex bytes with open rounds: line 25 "DO" = D0, line 36 "CO" = 00,
!     line 44 "DC" = D0, line 48 "CD" = 0D -- all by what the statement
!     assembles to; octal "C" fields are 0.  line 8's "0C" is a real C.
!   * "VSET3-C.32" (lines 22, 25) = VSET3-0.32.
!   * line 19 prints "LV,VT3,VX+VWT-": the "-" is the COMMENT MARK, an
!     empty comment, not a minus.  C28-6129 PDF p.5: "The beginning of a
!     comment is signaled by the character ' (an 8-4 double punch)",
!     example "TABLE' BEGIN CONVERSION" -- no blank before it; this drum
!     prints ' as "-" (the remark column).  Written VX+VWT.
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run ?B000071 .. ?B000105 (prefix
! glyph round, as in the header).  Shared: 73 (lines 3/4), 75 (6/7),
! 77 (9/10), 78 (11/12), 79 (13/14/15), 80 (16/17), 81 (18/19),
! 82 (20/21), 83 (22/23), 86 (26/27/28), 87 (29/30), 88 (31/32/33),
! 90 (35/36), 91 (37/38), 92 (39/40), 93 (41/42), 103 (52/53),
! 104 (54/55).  No serial is skipped.

